<onlyinclude>'''Open-source software''' is software distributed under a license that permits users to inspect, use, modify and redistribute its source code under defined conditions.

== Explanation ==
Open source is not simply software whose code can be viewed. The license must grant specified freedoms. Projects can be maintained by volunteers, companies or mixed communities, and open-source software may be sold. Different licenses impose different conditions when modifications are distributed.

